 "purpose": "The topics 'Tijd, geld en snelheid' (time, money and speed): quantities that do not (only) work with the units table, plus the readers and writers of durations and clock times.",
 "details": "Time works with 60 (not 100), the place where children go wrong and where the thinking errors look. A duration is typed as '2 u 15 min' and a clock time as '11.15 u'; lees_duur and lees_klok parse them (minutes, or minutes after midnight), duur_tekst and klok_tekst write them, and klok_cijfers shows what the digital clock display (terminal/digitaal.py) shows while the child types. Three topics share a base _Grootheid (klad on, cheat sheet, reader that ignores the euro sign): Tijd (convert units, mixed hours and minutes, duration between two times, arrival time), Geld (euro and cent, change, a purchase of two fruits) and Snelheid (distance, time, speed in km/u and m/s). Each has a worked solution in klad lines. Note: DINGEN here (things to buy) has the same name as, but different content from, DINGEN in procenten.py.",
 "module_docstring": "Tijd, geld en snelheid: grootheden die niet (alleen) met de eenhedentabel werken.",
